text\n\nThis is a Go service - vulnerabilities in HTTP handlers are remotely exploitable.\n\n## Changes\n- `hscontrol/templates/register_confirm.go`\n\n## Behavior Preservation\nThe change is scoped to 1 file on the vulnerable path; it only tightens handling of untrusted input and leaves valid inputs unaffected.\n\n## Security Invariant\n> **Property**: The security boundary is maintained under adversarial input\n\n<details>\n<summary>Regression test</summary>\n\n```go\npackage templates_test\n\nimport (\n\t\"testing\"\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"html/template\"\n\t\n\t\"github.com/juanfont/headscale/hscontrol/templates\"\n)\n\nfunc TestRegisterConfirmInputSanitization(t *testing.T) {\n\tpayloads := []string{\n\t\t// Valid input\n\t\t\"normal-user-input\",\n\t\t// Boundary case - maximum length typical for form inputs\n\t\t\"very-long-input-that-exceeds-typical-form-limits-and-could-cause-buffer-overflow-or-dos-if-not-handled-properly-by-the-template-rendering-engine\",\n\t\t// Adversarial payload - HTML injection attempt\n\t\t\"<script>alert('xss')</script><img src=x onerror=alert(1)>\",\n\t\t// Adversarial payload - Template injection attempt\n\t\t\"{{.Execute}} {{printf \\\"%s\\\" \\\"injection\\\"}}\",\n\t\t// Adversarial payload - SQL/NoSQL injection pattern\n\t\t\"'; DROP TABLE users; -- {\\\"$ne\\\": null}\",\n\t}\n\n\tfor _, payload := range payloads {\n\t\tt.Run(payload, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\t// Create template data with adversarial input\n\t\t\tdata := struct {\n\t\t\t\tUserInput string\n\t\t\t}{\n\t\t\t\tUserInput: payload,\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t// Execute the actual template from production code\n\t\t\ttmpl, err := template.New(\"register_confirm\").Parse(templates.RegisterConfirm)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Failed to parse template: %v\", err)\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tvar buf bytes.Buffer\n\t\t\terr = tmpl.Execute(&buf, data)\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t// Security property: Template execution must not panic or crash\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"Template execution failed (may be expected for invalid input): %v\", err)\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t// Security property: Output must not contain unescaped adversarial payload\n\t\t\toutput := buf.String()\n\t\t\tif output != \"\" {\n\t\t\t\t// Check that script tags are properly escaped/removed\n\t\t\t\tif containsUnsafeHTML(output, payload) {\n\t\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"Template output contains potentially unsafe content from payload: %s\", payload)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n\n// Helper to check for unsafe HTML in output\nfunc containsUnsafeHTML(output, payload string) bool {\n\t// Check if dangerous patterns appear unescaped in output\n\tdangerousPatterns := []string{\n\t\t\"<script>\",\n\t\t\"onerror=\",\n\t\t\"onload=\",\n\t\t\"javascript:\",\n\t\t\"{{.Execute\",\n\t\t\"'; DROP TABLE\",\n\t}\n\t\n\tfor _, pattern := range dangerousPatterns {\n\t\tif bytes.Contains([]byte(output), []byte(pattern)) {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}}}\n```\n\n</details>\n\nThis test guards against regressions — it's useful independent of the code change above.\n\n---\n*This patch removes an exploit primitive — a code pattern that, while not independently exploitable today, could be chained with other weaknesses by automated exploit-development tooling. Proactive removal of such primitives raises the bar against increasingly capable automated attack tools.*\n\n---\n*Automated security fix by [OrbisAI Security](https://orbisappsec.com)*\n","created_at":"2026-08-09T12:54:25Z","updated_at":"2026-08-09T13:45:51Z","closed_at":"2026-08-09T13:45:50Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"1ea12ff1af9a581f97b9b38529d44878d217fffa","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https:/